          "id": "11f569595f8821352c3ad2c126bfc995c07d1a3b",
          "message": "Qt6.2.2 (#969)\n\n* Move to Qt 6.2.2\r\n\r\n* Update CMake\r\n\r\n* Update cmake formatting\r\n\r\n* Old CMake formatting\r\n\r\n* More CMake fixes\r\n\r\n* Dummy out Dbus\r\n\r\nLet's see if the Mac version will build now\r\n\r\n* Reformat cmake\r\n\r\n* More Formatting\r\n\r\n* Debug Mac build\r\n\r\n* Correct debugging variables\r\n\r\n* So they've moved Qt6\r\n\r\n* Where did they move qt 6.2.2 to ?\r\n\r\n* Pointlessly move Qt on mac\r\n\r\n* Format cmake again\r\n\r\n* Update qt directory for PrepDMG\r\n\r\n* Try and force C++17 on Windows\r\n\r\n* Force __cplusplus in in MSVC\r\n\r\n* Brute force the MSVC compile option\r\n\r\n* Try to force Windows to recognise that we want c++17.\r\n\r\n* Trying new windows 2022 build\r\n\r\n* Build for MSVC 2022\r\n\r\n* Update windows conan compiler version\r\n\r\n* Try and localise the compile flags for C++17 on Qt\r\n\r\n* Cmake formatting\r\n\r\n* Add MSVC fix to more gui packages\r\n\r\n* More MSVC fixes\r\n\r\n* Try and fix MSVC in modules\r\n\r\n* Fix msvc on modulewidgetproducer",
